<title>POLAND: Zloty fixed flat at -1.07 pct from parity rate.</title>
<headline>Zloty fixed flat at -1.07 pct from parity rate.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-08-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>The National Bank of Poland fixed the zloty at 3.4710 to the dollar, up from 3.4870 on Thursday and at 1.9065 to the mark, down from 1.9000, the NBP said.</p>
<p>The central bank fixed the zloty at an average of -1.07 percent from the weighted dollar and mark parity rates, flat from Thursday, the last trading day last week.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
